From f8370960f32a8861e1d0fea7be09e79eade33a4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cohost u2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:51:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Inline fixed-arity calls of jit_functions at -O3; inline var
 deref; one-allocation rest args

Draft: cohost doc/upstream/jank-24-direct-calls.md.
Repro: bash dev/research/upstream/run.sh 24-direct-calls (in johnmn3/cohost.cljc).

1. -Odirect-call, now real and the default at -O3 (-Ono-direct-call turns it
   off; off at -O0..2): a dynamic call compiles to jank::runtime::call_fast(f,
   args...), an always-inline helper in jit_function.hpp that calls a
   jit_function's fixed arity through its arity pointer (no virtual call, no
   small-number tag tests) and falls back to object_ref::call for anything else
   (variadic fns, keywords, maps, a missing arity). The fn object is read at
   every call, so def again, alter-var-root, with-redefs and binding are seen
   at once and no per-var redefinition flag is needed.
2. Compiled var derefs call var::deref_inline(): the root load inline when the
   var was never thread-bound, else deref().
3. multi_function calls its dispatch fn and the resolved method through
   call_fast.
4. jit_variadic_function builds a call's rest args with
   native_array_sequence::create_packed: the sequence and its elements in one
   GC allocation instead of two.

